<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Malik al-Rahim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1048">1048</a>–<a href="/years/1055">1055</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Malik al-Rahim was the last Buyid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-kalijar">Abu Kalijar</a> in 1048. Unable to control his Turkish troops or his brothers, he lost authority to the military commander al-Basasiri. In December 1055 the Seljuk ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughril">Tughril Beg</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, was recognised as sultan by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Qa'im and imprisoned al-Malik al-Rahim, ending Buyid rule in Iraq; he died in captivity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-malik-al-rahim.jpg" alt="al-Malik al-Rahim" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iraq_Ninth_Century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
